# Toolchain — WPNest

## Commands

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Dev server | `npm run dev` |
| Production build | `npm run build` |
| JS lint | `npm run lint:js` |
| JS lint + fix | `npm run lint:js:fix` |
| CSS lint | `npm run lint:css` |
| CSS lint + fix | `npm run lint:css:fix` |
| PHP lint | `npm run phpcs` |
| PHP auto-fix | `npm run phpcbf` |

> **Note:** There are no SCSS lint commands. The project uses Tailwind CSS v4.
> CSS linting targets `sources/**/*.css` via Stylelint.

## Run After Changes

| Changed | Commands to run |
|---|---|
| PHP | `npm run phpcs` |
| JavaScript | `npm run lint:js` → `npm run build` |
| CSS / Tailwind | `npm run lint:css` → `npm run build` |
| New ACF block | PHP + CSS + JS checks + `npm run build` |

## Tailwind v4 Build Notes

- The Tailwind CSS v4 plugin (`@tailwindcss/vite`) runs as part of the Vite build.
- Content scanning is configured via `@source` directives in `sources/css/style.css` — no `tailwind.config.js` needed.
- The compiled CSS is output to `assets/css/style-[hash].css` and referenced via `assets/.vite/manifest.json`.
- `themeCSS('main.css')` in `includes/theme-scripts.php` reads the manifest key `sources/css/style.css`.

## Rules

- Fix all lint/test errors before completion.
- Don't disable lint rules without justification.
- Ensure `npm run build` completes successfully.
